{
  "name": "Google Sheets: schedule Social Poster posts from ready rows",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ed5b6a04-b0e5-4213-a778-cfb067ae361c",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis workflow helps you process planned social posts from a Google Sheet. A schedule reads the sheet on a regular interval and keeps only rows with status `ready` and a filled-in caption. For each of those rows, Social Poster creates a draft, schedules it at least five minutes in the future, and confirms it for publishing. The workflow then writes the draft reference and status `scheduled` back to the sheet. If scheduling fails, it writes status `error` so you can check the row and set it to `ready` again. There is no immediate publishing. If your team requires approval, the post waits in Social Poster under “Waiting for you”.\n\n### Setup\nThis template uses the unverified community node `n8n-nodes-social-poster` (tested with version 0.1.1). It runs on self-hosted n8n only, not on n8n Cloud. Install it under Settings → Community Nodes → Install, package name `n8n-nodes-social-poster`. Guide: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/\nCreate credentials for “Social Poster API” and Google Sheets (OAuth2). Create the Social Poster key under the account menu → AI access → API key for n8n. Base URL: `https://app.social-poster.io`.\nCreate a sheet with these headers in row 1: `Caption`, `Link`, `MediaURLs`, `Title`, `Status`, `DraftRef`, `ScheduledAt`. In “Settings”, enter the spreadsheet ID, sheet name, account reference (`acc_…`) and minutes until publishing (at least 5). Select both credentials, put a test row on status `ready`, run once, and check Social Poster before you activate the schedule.\n\n### Customization\nYou can change the interval or create a draft only instead of scheduling. Do not set too many rows to `ready` at once; the API key limits publishing steps (3 per minute). Leave “X Content Reviewed” off until a person has checked the exact text and media for X (Twitter).",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dcda949e-ff7a-4704-bb7b-cf4b82e07db7",
      "name": "Schedule and settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Values you must set\nSet the interval, spreadsheet ID, sheet name, account reference and lead time in minutes here.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
